SUMMARY:Third Friday with Laurie Zuckerman\, Finn Eichler and The Ministry of Cardboard!
DESCRIPTION:Meet our artists and enjoy the Scrap Exchange Pop Up installation!\nLaurie Zuckerman is a textile artist who will join us with her textile patches\, textile wall art and textile gift tags! Laurie’s fabrics are often from The Scrap Exchange! She states\, “Part of what I love about the Scrap Exchange is never knowing what I’ll find. A piece of upholstery fabric\, a ripped sari\, or an unusual bead or piece of yarn can end up determining what a bird’s wing looks like or sending a piece in an entirely new direction.” \nFinn Eicher is a 16 year old entrepreneur and creative that has honed his skills with 3D printing! Meet Finn and explore his work that includes things like fidgets\, connect 4 games and action figures. They are all incredible and here are descriptions of a few things you will see! Finn will bring his 3D printer so you can see it in action! \nThe Scrap Exchange has a Pop-up Art Installation | “The Ministry of Cardboard” by Jason Lord\nAfter four months of transforming The Scrap Exchange’s Cameron Gallery\, artist Jason Lord brings a pop-up version of his immersive installation\, “The Ministry of Cardboard\,” to The Artisan Market at 305 and Durham Sculpture Studio for Third Friday.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/third-friday-with-laurie-zuckerman-finn-eichler-and-the-ministry-of-cardboard/
LOCATION:The Artisan Market at 305\, 305 E. Chapel Hill Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art,Craft,Third Friday
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Pink-Minimalist-Fashion-Moodboard-Pinterest-Pin-1.jpg
