SUMMARY:Ragie Ban at The Fruit
DESCRIPTION:Morning Choir presents Brazil’s rising tech house phenomenon RAGIE BAN for a night of infectious grooves and underground innovation. At just 22\, this São Paulo native has already achieved massive career milestones with his gritty yet groovy\, dark but danceable signature sound. With 1.3 million monthly Spotify listeners and over 13 million total streams\, his innovative productions have earned backing from Michael Bibi\, Mochakk\, Chris Lake\, Diplo\, Dennis Cruz\, and Vintage Culture. His 2025 collaboration “Toxic” with Chris Lake hit #1 on Beatport’s overall chart\, cementing his name among the genre’s elite. His impressive discography spans Revival NYC\, Shout Label\, Nervous\, CUFF\, and Hellbent Records with tracks like “Dangerous\,” “Let’s Go Deep\,” and “MonkeyMonkey” showcasing his deep understanding of the dancefloor. Ragie’s high-impact DJ sets and festival mainstage presence represent the kind of boundary-pushing artistry that’s positioning him as a defining voice of the next generation. From Brazilian warehouses to Durham’s most intimate setting\, he’s bringing the infectious energy and underground innovation that’s earned him international recognition as one of Brazil’s most exciting electronic exports. This is tech house as cultural evolution. Expect gritty basslines\, groovy rhythms\, and the kind of innovative production that’s earned co-signs from every major player in the scene.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/ragie-ban-at-the-fruit/
LOCATION:The Fruit\, 305 South Dillard St\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ragie-Ban-at-The-Fruit.jpeg
ORGANIZER;CN="Morning Choir":MAILTO:sean@morningchoir.com
GEO:35.9906486;-78.8966359
